    <!-- FAQ answers: one non-blank line per bullet (parsed in FaqScreen; not string-arrays — avoids AAPT2 crashes). -->
    <string name="faq_answer_rule_not_working">Check that the rule has a **name**, **source folder**, **destination folder**, and **file types**.
Tap any **highlighted folder path** and **grant access** again.
Switch to **All files access** if you use **Download**, **storage roots**, or many folders.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_folder_access_denied">This usually happens after **switching access mode**, **restoring a backup**, or **revoking folder permission**.
Tap the folder in **Edit Rule** and **grant access** again.
If the path looks like a **root-style** folder, switch to **All files access** in Settings.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_files_not_moving_automatically">Check that the rule is **enabled**.
Check that a **schedule** is set if you expect **automatic runs**.
Check **battery restrictions**, **folder access**, and **file filters**.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_cant_add_downloads_folder">**Select Folders Only** mode cannot grant the **Downloads** root or some **storage roots**.
Switch to **Full Access** in Settings, then pick folders or paths as needed.
Alternatively, choose a **subfolder inside Downloads** with the system picker if you stay on Selective Access.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_create_rule">Pick one or more **source folders**.
Pick a **destination folder** and add the **file types** to match.
**Save** the rule, then use **Preview** or **Simulate** before relying on it.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_rule_skipping_files">The file may not match the rule\'s **file types** or **advanced filters**.
The **destination** may already contain the same file and your **conflict mode** may **skip** it.
The file may be **outside** the selected folder scope if **access was lost**.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_what_simulate_does">**Simulate** previews what the rule **would do**.
**No files** are moved or copied during preview.
Use it to confirm **filters**, **destination**, and **folder access** before saving or running.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_scheduled_rules">**Scheduled rules** run in the **background** based on the **time** you choose.
The rule still needs **valid folder access** and **matching files**.
**Preview** the rule first so **automation** uses the setup you expect.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_rule_did_not_run">Check that the **schedule** is enabled and the rule itself is **enabled**.
Check **Android battery restrictions** and **notification-related** background limits.
Check that **folder access** is still valid and the rule still **finds matching files**.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_schedule_notifications">FilePipe does not post a notification for **every scheduled run** by default; check **Run history** to confirm runs.
Turn on **notifications** in **Settings** and allow them in **Android app settings** if you expect alerts.
**Battery saver** and **background restrictions** can delay or skip work; exclude FilePipe where needed.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_data_privacy">FilePipe works on-device.
Your files are not uploaded or tracked.
The app only acts on the rules you create.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_why_storage_access">FilePipe needs folder access to scan, move, or copy the files your rules target.
Selective Access limits FilePipe to the folders you approve.
All files access is required for Downloads, storage roots, and file-system paths.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_backup_contents">Backups include rules, history, and settings.
Folder permissions are not restored from backup.
After restore, review any rule with highlighted folder paths.</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_permissions_after_restore">Tap each affected folder and grant access again if you use Selective Access.
Re-enable All files access in Android settings if your rules use that mode.
Use the edit screen highlights to quickly see which folders need attention.</string>

